<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/harness/engine/shares',
        '/harness/engine/duration-of',
        '/harness/engine/measures-named',
        '/harness/measure/measure',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/harness/e2e/engine.spec.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the four counters move, and forced layout distinguishes'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/e2e/TopDeals.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the sort is a share of the click'"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Trace one click in Chromium">
        <p>Call <code>traceOp</code> from a Playwright test and do the op inside the body. The
            trace holds what the engine did over it and the page's user timing.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { traceOp } from '@abide/harness/engine'
            import { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'

            test('ranking by idle days restyles the list', async ({ page }) => {
                await page.goto('reports')
                const trace = await traceOp(page, 'rank by idle', async () => {
                    await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Most idle' }).click()
                })
                expect(trace.counters.recalcStyle).toBeGreaterThan(0)
                expect(trace.counters.layout).toBeGreaterThan(0)
            })
        `} />
        <p>The trace is read over the DevTools protocol, so <code>traceOp</code> runs in
            Chromium only.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Catch a layout a read forced">
        <p>A layout read after a write forces the layout the write invalidated.
            <code>forcedLayout</code> counts those, apart from the layouts the frame does.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            const trace = await traceOp(page, 'widen columns', async () => {
                await page.evaluate(() => {
                    for (const cell of document.querySelectorAll('td')) {
                        cell.style.paddingLeft = '8px'
                        void cell.offsetWidth
                    }
                })
            })
            expect(trace.counters.forcedLayout).toBeGreaterThan(0)
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
